SUMMARY:Book Launch
DESCRIPTION:Australia lost the war. Now Tess must face spirits from the pas
 t\, a mysterious new boy in town and The Wall. The Wall Within\, by Laura 
 Morris is a story of survival\, friendship\, and hidden power - where one 
 girl’s discovery could unravel everything. Laura will be in conversation
  with local legends\, Roz Mackay and Pat Cavanagh. Attendees can look forw
 ard to a bookish afternoon of chats\, readings\, bedazzling and “shimmer
 ing” as we journey into the world of Tess and Raze. Buy some delicious f
 ood and enjoy some drinks at Canteen Kitchen + Bar\, and join Laura as she
  shares her journey to becoming a YA debut author. Age attendance: 13+ Abo
 ut Laura: Laura Morris is an author and Coolum local. Her writing has appe
 ared in QLD Writers’ Centre’s Pen and Pixel magazine\, and her short s
 tory Tarnished is published in the 2025 Sydney Hammond Memorial Short Stor
 y Competition anthology. Her debut novel\, The Wall Within (published by H
 awkeye Publishing)\, made the shortlist of QWC’s Publishable program in 
 2022\, and the longlist of the Hawkeye Manuscript Development Prize for 20
 25. Laura has a Bachelor of Arts from the University of Qld and a Graduate
  Certificate in Creative Writing from the University of the Sunshine Coast
 . She grew up in Ipswich and Brisbane\, and now lives on the Sunshine Coas
 t with her family. She loves writing\, gardening\, Game Fit Tennis\, and P
 ickleball. Follow LauraMorrisWriter on TikTok\, Instagram and Facebook.
LOCATION:Canteen Kitchen + Bar\, Coolum Beach\, QLD 4573
URL:https://www.trybooking.com/events/landing/1608584
